y exists on the latest slate.</p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <section class=\"stats-grid\" id=\"overview-cards\"></section>\r\n      </section>\r\n\r\n      <section class=\"two-up\">\r\n        <article class=\"panel\">\r\n          <div class=\"section-head\">\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"eyebrow\">2026 season</p>\r\n              <h2>Top 5 home run leaders</h2>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"table-wrap\" id=\"leaderboard-table\"></div>\r\n        </article>\r\n\r\n        <article class=\"panel\">\r\n          <div class=\"section-head\">\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"eyebrow\">Yesterday</p>\r\n              <h2>Full slate recap</h2>\r\n              <p class=\"section-note\">Show the whole prior slate, not just the winners.</p>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"yesterday-summary\" id=\"yesterday-summary\"></div>\r\n          <div class=\"table-wrap\" id=\"yesterday-table\"></div>\r\n        </article>\r\n      </section>\r\n\r\n      <section class=\"panel\">\r\n        <div class=\"section-head\">\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">Confidence</p>\r\n            <h2>Tier performance</h2>\r\n            <p class=\"section-note\">These numbers summarize how each confidence band has performed since public tracking began, with elite treated as the most selective subset of the public board.</p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"table-wrap\" id=\"confidence-table\"></div>\r\n      </section>\r\n\r\n      <section class=\"panel\" id=\"lineups\">\r\n        <div class=\"section-head\">\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">Lineups</p>\r\n            <h2>Projected and Confirmed Lineups</h2>\r\n            <p class=\"section-note\">Only games tied to current published picks are shown here. Pregame publishes use projected lineups until MLB posts confirmed lineups.</p>\r\n        